## §3. EVIDENCE & DOCUMENTATION

### 3.1 Evidence Contract

Each phase produces exactly one evidence file under `docs/reports/plans/`.

**Commands executed via:** `subprocess.run(argv, shell=False, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")`
**PowerShell invocation is FORBIDDEN.**
**File-based Python scripts REQUIRED for complex analysis** — write to `ops_scripts/ci/` or `tools/evidence/`, then execute via subprocess. Never inline Python via PowerShell.

Evidence files MUST be ASCII-only with ANSI escape sequences stripped.

### 3.2 Required Evidence Sections

**Required sections (in order):**
1. `# <Phase Title>`
2. `## Scope` — with graph justification
3. `## INSPECTED_FILES`
4. `## FACT_CLASSIFICATION` — three tiers: DIRECTLY OBSERVED / DERIVED / UNRESOLVED
5. Command output sections
6. `## DEPENDENCY_GRAPH` — roots, impacted nodes, upstream set, downstream set, edge classes, boundary/cycle findings, reason each changed file is in scope
7. `## BRANCH_INVENTORY`
8. `## ROBUSTNESS_MATRIX` — success/edge/failure/recovery/determinism/side-effect tests per changed surface
9. `## DEFECT_MODEL`

**Conditional sections (add when applicable):**
- `## TIMEOUT_RECOVERY` — when timeout occurs (§5.4)
- `## CLUSTER_ANALYSIS` — for every repair (§2.5)
- `## FAILURE_CAPTURE` — before any repair edit (§2.5)
- `## PROOF_ARTIFACT_TRUTHFULNESS` — when ADG proof artifact referenced (§2.4)
- `## POLICY_DRIFT` — when policy regression classified (§6.1)
- `## CONTRACT_CONFLICT` — when contract conflict identified (§6.2)
- `## ENVIRONMENT_CONTRACT` — when environment dependency involved (§6.3)

### 3.3 Three-Tier Fact Classification

| Tier | Label | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `DIRECTLY OBSERVED` | Read directly from raw artifact/command stdout — no inference |
| 2 | `DERIVED` | Computed from secondary command — source command MUST be named |
| 3 | `UNRESOLVED` | Not yet proven — MUST be listed explicitly, never omitted |

A phase MUST NOT be declared complete while `Unresolved` is non-empty, unless each item is deferred to a named future phase.

### 3.4 Forbidden Evidence Patterns

- ❌ DERIVED fact without naming the deriving command
- ❌ Omitting UNRESOLVED facts — silence is not proof of absence
- ❌ Upgrading DERIVED to DIRECTLY OBSERVED without re-running primary source
- ❌ Claiming phase complete while UNRESOLVED items remain

### 3.5 Artifact Links

Every artifact reference in a response MUST use backtick citation format: `` `@<absolute_path>` ``. Plain text paths = CONSTITUTIONAL VIOLATION.

### 3.6 Artifact Location

All plans, evidence, and reports MUST reside in: `docs/reports/plans/`

All Python file I/O MUST use `encoding="utf-8"`. Evidence files are raw execution captures, ASCII-only.

