## §5. CI ENFORCEMENT FRAMEWORK

### 5.1 Single Entrypoint

`python ops_scripts/ci/run_contract_gates.py` enforces all gates. CI MUST fail immediately on any violation.

### 5.2 Critical Infrastructure Fail-Closed

Critical infrastructure MUST fail-closed. No graceful fallbacks, silent degradation, or best-effort modes.

**Critical infrastructure:** BGE embeddings, AST dependency graph (§2.6), test execution (§1.4), SSOT configuration (§7.2).

FORBIDDEN: `try/except` that catches from critical components and returns None/empty/default; conditional logic providing alternatives when critical components unavailable; `logger.warning()` followed by `pass` for critical operations.

### 5.3 Query Timeout & Progress Reporting

All queries, searches, and long-running operations MUST have explicit timeout parameters and fail-closed behavior on timeout.

**Timeout ranges:** Fast (grep, file reads, simple AST): 5–30s | Medium (graph construction, test collection): 30–120s | Heavy (full repo analysis): 120–600s | External API: 10–60s.

Operations >5s MUST provide progress reporting (percentage, current item, ETA) at least every 5s.

When timeout occurs: use ADG to isolate the bottleneck, identify root cause, rerun with targeted scope, document recovery in `## TIMEOUT_RECOVERY`. Fail-closed: if ADG cannot be built or bottleneck not identified → raise original TimeoutError.

### 5.4 CI Integrity Gates

CI MUST fail immediately on any of:

| # | Condition |
|---|---|
| 1 | Required phase artifact missing from `docs/reports/plans/` |
| 2 | `FACT_CLASSIFICATION` missing or has UNRESOLVED items |
| 3 | Broad pytest run before final phase |
| 4 | Unexpected skip or xfail not in skip registry (§1.4) |
| 5 | Failing test without `FAILURE_CAPTURE` record (§2.5) |
| 6 | ADG schema mapping changed mid-run (schema freeze violated) |
| 7 | Edit commit timestamp before cluster artifact timestamp |
| 8 | Test strictness weakened (assertion removed, `assert True` added, mock broadened) |
| 9 | `repair_class` missing from commit touching production code |
| 10 | Governance module touched with `production_bug_fix` without `POLICY_DRIFT` section |
| 11 | Two conflicting contracts touched without `CONTRACT_CONFLICT` section |
| 12 | subprocess/vLLM/CUDA failure without `ENVIRONMENT_CONTRACT` section |
| 13 | "repair complete" claimed without post-repair full-suite green artifact |

