## §7. ACCEPTANCE DISCIPLINE

Acceptance criteria MUST be deterministic, command-exact, exit-code-exact, count-exact. Forbidden language: "should", "expected to", "approximately", "equivalent". Criteria immutable once phase begins.

### 7.1 Forbidden Overclaiming Vocabulary

| Forbidden claim | Required condition |
|---|---|
| "tests are present" | Raw ADG entity count `tests > 0` |
| "fixtures are present" | Raw ADG entity count `fixtures > 0` |
| "convergence achieved" | All five §7.2 conditions met |
| "repair complete" | All six §7.3 conditions met |
| "repo is healthy" | Post-repair full-suite green (zero fails, errors, unexpected skips) |
| "no dependencies" | ADG explicitly returned empty edge set |
| "directly observed" | Fact read directly from raw artifact — no inference |

Using these phrases without the listed condition = CONSTITUTIONAL VIOLATION.

### 7.2 Convergence Declaration (Scoped Claim Only)

ALL five conditions must hold simultaneously:
1. Active scoped failures = 0
2. Unregistered skips = 0
3. No expired registry entries
4. `FACT_CLASSIFICATION.Unresolved` is empty
5. Scope lossiness documented (if file-level fallback used)

### 7.3 Repair Run Completion (Six Conditions)

1. All §7.2 scoped convergence conditions met
2. Every ADG-reachable dependent of repaired surface executed and passed
3. Full pytest suite green — zero failures, errors, unexpected skips
4. Full-suite run timestamp LATER THAN last repair commit timestamp
5. No new failures introduced (count ≤ pre-repair baseline)
6. Final summary artifact in `docs/reports/plans/` with empty `Unresolved`

